      "content": "No, taking a double dose of Benadryl is unsafe due to the risk of severe side effects like extreme drowsiness or heart issues, and it will not resolve a true allergic reaction if you are allergic cross-reacted. The symptoms of hives, redness, and throat tightness combined with potential allergic foods are classic signs of anaphylaxis that require emergency medical attention regardless of your initial anxiety. Please call 911 immediately or go to the nearest emergency room so professionals can assess your throat and provide the necessary treatment.",
