    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Using an asthma inhaler for allergic reactions is dangerous and ineffective because albuterol only treats wheezing caused by narrowed airways, not the swelling of throat tissues caused by allergies. Swallowing a double or triple dose of Benadryl can cause life-threatening heart problems and severe breathing difficulties that will make you worse instead of better. You must go to the emergency room immediately because the cost and financial hardship are irrelevant when your life is at risk; paramedics can check your condition for free or with minimal cost while you wait for the hospital.",
